course: dictionary
lesson: 15255
title: New word: shortfall
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A shortfall is the amount by which something is less than what is needed or expected. The word is built from short and fall: you have fallen short of your goal. «The class raised £165 for the trip, but it costs £200.» The class has £165 and needs £200, so there is a shortfall.
explain: To find a shortfall in maths, take what you have away from what you need. Need minus have equals shortfall. £200 minus £165 is £35, so the shortfall is £35.
explain: The word is common in news and business. «The bakery had a shortfall of flour, so it could not make all the bread.» The bakery needed more flour than it had, so it did not have enough to make everything. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "not enough flour" still makes sense.
fact: Shortfall means an amount by which something is less than what is needed or expected.
fact: To find a shortfall, subtract: what you need minus what you have.
fact: «The shop had a shortfall of ten boxes of apples» means there were ten boxes fewer than needed.
fact: Shortfall is a noun. One is a shortfall, and more than one is shortfalls.
fact: In news and business, a shortfall often means not enough money, food or staff.
exercise: «The class raised £165, but the trip costs £200.» What is the shortfall? | £165 | £200 | *£35 | £365
exercise: «The bakery had a shortfall of flour, so it could not make all the bread.» What does shortfall mean here? | *Not enough flour for what was needed | Too much flour in the store | Flour that arrived early | A new kind of bread
exercise: «The team needed 12 players but had only 9.» How many players is the shortfall? | *3 | 12 | 21 | 9
test: The shop expected to sell 50 cakes but sold 38. What is the shortfall? | 38 | *12 | 88 | 50
test: What is the best meaning of shortfall? | *An amount that is less than what is needed | A sudden loud noise | A kind of shoe | An amount that is more than expected
exam: A school needs £500 for a new library and has raised £420. What is the shortfall? | £920 | £500 | £420 | *£80, which is £500 minus £420
